# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This guide walks you through getting started with the GOV.UK Content API to retrieve
content by making a GET request to the API.

## Who this is for

You can use this guide if you are a developer or a non-developer who understands
the basics of [APIs][api-def].

## Before you start

Make sure you have one of the following tools available:

- a terminal with a data transfer utility, such as [curl][curl]
- a dedicated API client such as the [Postman][postman-install] app

## Authentication

You do not need to authenticate to use the GOV.UK Content API.

## Base URL

The base URL for all requests to the GOV.UK Content API is:

```txt
https://www.gov.uk/api/content/
```

## Make your first API request

To make your first request to the GOV.UK Content API:

1. Choose a page on the GOV.UK website, for example: [https://www.gov.uk/take-pet-abroad](https://www.gov.uk/take-pet-abroad).
2. Make a note of the URL component after the domain, which for our example is:
   `/take-pet-abroad`.
   This is the **path** for which you'll retrieve the content from the API.
3. Add this path to the end of the API [Base URL](#base-url) to create the complete
   **API URL**, which for our example is [`https://www.gov.uk/api/content/take-pet-abroad`](https://www.gov.uk/api/content/take-pet-abroad).
4. Using your preferred tool, make a GET request to this API URL. For example,
   use the curl utility in the terminal:
   <pre><code class="language-shell">curl https://www.gov.uk/api/content/take-pet-abroad</code></pre>
5. Alternatively, you can use a dedicated tool such as the Postman app to make
   the GET request.
   Look at the Postman [quick start][postman-quick-start] guide for how to do
   this, using the API URL for the request.
6. You’ll receive a JSON response and the fields for this are
   explained in the [reference documentation](reference.html).

